{"text": "SEP @5 '97 @4:31PM PHILIP MORRIS\n\n=\u2014==PERS\n\nLegal office\nP.O. Box 942707\nmento, CA. 64220-2707\n\u2018Telecommunications Device for the Dest - (916) 326-1260\n(016) 328-3675\nFAX (@16) 326-3659\n\nVIA TELEFAX\n\nSeptember 4, 1997\n\nG, Penn Holsenbeck\nVice President, Associate Generat Counsel\n\u2018and Corporate Secretary\nPhilip Morris Companies, inc,\n120 Park Avenue\nNew York, NY 10017-5592\n\nDear Penn:\n\nEnclosed is a copy of a letter from California Assemblyman Wally Knox. Assemblyman\nKnox Is the Chair of our Committee on Public Employees, Retirement and Social\nSecurity. As indicated in his letter, this Committee is holding @ hearing on\nSeptember 19, 1997 conceming the investment by California's public pension funds in\ntobacco stocks. Because CalPERS is a large holder of Philip Morris stock, we believe\nyou may have an interest in attanding this hearing. Assemblyman Knox has asked us to\nconvay his invitation to you, or anather company representative, to attend. We would\n\u2018appreciate your giving his invitation serious consideration.\n\nPlease let me know your response as soon as possible. You may also wish to contact,\nAssemblyman Knox at (916) 322-4320. Again, thank you for your cooperation.\n\nSincerely,\n\nagg Bek\n\nKAYLA J. GILLAN\nGeneral Counsel\n\nEnclosure\n\ncc: Assemblyman Wally Knox\nJames E, Burton\n\nCalifornia Public Employees\u2019 Retirement System\nLincoln Plaza - 400 P Street - Sacramento, CA 95814\n\n2826 ro 220z",
